From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:56:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: loader splash, write the spinner inside its image
 buffer

Fixes a loader panic on every boot-video graphics boot ("zfree(...):
corrupt memlist2" right after "Start @", seen in an x86_64 UTM/QEMU VM).

gfx.fb_putmask() (patch 0014) recolours the spinner PNG in place up to
png.png_datalen. pnglite sets png_datalen to the inflated IDAT size,
width * height * bpp + height (one filter byte per row), but png.image is
only width * height * bpp. The loop wrote height bytes past the end of
the image, over the next heap node, and the next free() found the
corrupt free list during bi_load().

- fb_putmask() bounds the loop by width * height * 4.
- build_splash_module() copies width * height * bpp bytes of the logo,
  not png_datalen (that over-read was in the stock code; the kernel uses
  the splash_info dimensions).

Text, serial and CI boots never run either path.

Carried out-of-tree for NextBSD.
---
 stand/common/gfx_fb.c    |  8 ++++++--
 stand/liblua/gfx_utils.c | 10 ++++++++--
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/stand/common/gfx_fb.c b/stand/common/gfx_fb.c
index a8c7e5a..98b4c01 100644
--- a/stand/common/gfx_fb.c
+++ b/stand/common/gfx_fb.c
@@ -3247,8 +3247,12 @@ build_splash_module(vm_offset_t addr, int type)
 	addr += archsw.arch_copyin(&si, addr, sizeof (struct splash_info));
 	addr = roundup2(addr, 8);
 
-	/* Copy the bitmap. */
-	addr += archsw.arch_copyin(png.image, addr, png.png_datalen);
+	/*
+	 * Copy the bitmap: width * height * bpp bytes, the size of
+	 * png.image.  png_datalen is one filter byte per row larger.
+	 */
+	addr += archsw.arch_copyin(png.image, addr,
+	    png.width * png.height * png.bpp);
 	file_addmetadata(fp, MODINFOMD_SPLASH, sizeof(splashp), &splashp);
 
 	boot_splash_logo_w = png.width;
diff --git a/stand/liblua/gfx_utils.c b/stand/liblua/gfx_utils.c
index 0cb4f80..1ea6d33 100644
--- a/stand/liblua/gfx_utils.c
+++ b/stand/liblua/gfx_utils.c
@@ -340,7 +340,7 @@ lua_fb_putmask(lua_State *L)
 {
 	const char *name;
 	png_t png;
-	uint32_t x, y, i;
+	uint32_t x, y, i, len;
 	uint8_t r, g, b;
 	int ret = 0;
 
@@ -358,7 +358,13 @@ lua_fb_putmask(lua_State *L)
 
 	if (png_open(&png, name) == PNG_NO_ERROR) {
 		if (png.color_type == PNG_TRUECOLOR_ALPHA) {
-			for (i = 0; i + 3 < png.png_datalen; i += 4) {
+			/*
+			 * The decoded image is width * height * 4 bytes.
+			 * png_datalen is the inflated IDAT size, one filter
+			 * byte per row larger: never write up to it.
+			 */
+			len = png.width * png.height * 4;
+			for (i = 0; i + 3 < len; i += 4) {
 				png.image[i] = r;
 				png.image[i + 1] = g;
 				png.image[i + 2] = b;
-- 
